+# Cache Eviction Policy
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use Least Recently Used (LRU) cache eviction with a fixed time-to-live (TTL) of 300 seconds. Entries age out consistently after the TTL regardless of access patterns, and when eviction is needed the least recently accessed entries are removed first, which gives predictable cache behavior with simple semantics.
